course: dictionary
lesson: 4595
title: Herder: the person who looks after animals
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A herder is a person who looks after a group of animals, such as cattle, sheep, goats or reindeer. A herd is a group of animals kept together, so a herder is the person who takes care of that herd.
explain: A herder moves the animals to fresh grass and keeps them safe. «On the steppe, dry grassland too dry for crops in many places, and in deserts many peoples lived as nomadic herders, moving with their animals to find fresh grass and water.» The clues are moving, fresh grass and water, so a herder looks after animals and leads them to food.
explain: The word is often part of a longer name, such as «cattle herder», «goat herder» or «reindeer herder». The first word tells you which animals are looked after, so a reindeer herder looks after reindeer. Try your meaning in the sentence: «A reindeer herder found a baby mammoth» still makes sense, so you have the right idea.
fact: A herder is a person who looks after animals such as cattle, sheep, goats or reindeer.
fact: Herders move their animals to fresh grass and keep them safe.
fact: «Nomadic herders» move from place to place with their animals to find grass and water.
fact: In Bible stories, shepherds are herders who look after sheep.
fact: «Reindeer herder» means a person who looks after reindeer.
exercise: What does a herder do? | Sails boats across the sea | *Looks after a group of animals and moves them to fresh grass | Builds houses out of stone | Sells bread in a market
exercise: In the name «goat herder», which animals does the herder look after? | *Goats | Fish | Cows | Reindeer
exercise: «Many peoples lived as nomadic herders, moving with their animals.» Why did nomadic herders move? | *To find fresh grass and water for their animals | To sell their animals | To hide from the rain | To visit the shops
test: Who is a herder? | A machine that cuts grass | A person who never leaves home | A kind of mountain | *A person who looks after animals such as sheep or reindeer
test: «A baby mammoth was found almost whole by a reindeer herder in 2007.» Who found the mammoth? | *A person who looks after reindeer | A miner digging for gold | A scientist who makes freezers | A teacher from a school
exam: What is a «goat herder»? | A farmer who grows only wheat | *A person who looks after goats and moves them to fresh grass | A shop that sells goat milk | A builder of goat pens
